# Leak suppression policy: see README.md in this directory.

# pj_scripting/src/python_engine.cpp ensureInterpreter() retains
# py::scoped_interpreter and py::gil_scoped_release for the process lifetime.
# CPython is never finalized because doing so during static destruction is
# fragile; the released GIL lets every caller acquire it on its own thread.
# Observed: direct leaks of 16 and 1 bytes allocated in ensureInterpreter.
# ours-by-design: embedded interpreter guards, never finalized.
leak:ensureInterpreter

# Qt 6.11 QOpenGLWidget, when its context fails to create (the offscreen
# platform has no OpenGL: "QOpenGLWidget: Failed to create context"), drops the
# QOpenGLContext it allocated during the first resize. The context and its
# private point at each other, so LSan reports only indirect leaks: 760 bytes
# in 7 allocations, allocated from QOpenGLContext::QOpenGLContext under
# QOpenGLWidget::resizeEvent, no PJ4 frame. Suppressing the private also clears
# what it references. A QOpenGLWidget or QOpenGLContext that PJ4 itself leaks is
# still reported, through its own direct-leak stack.
# Observed: PlotWidgetCanvas.FlushTopWhenNotAlignedToScales,
# PlotCanvasContextRecreationGlTest, RasterTextGlTest (all skip without GL).
# third-party: Qt offscreen-platform context-failure path.
leak:QOpenGLContext::QOpenGLContext
